  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse d&#x2019;urgence aux cons&#xe9;quences sanitaires des inondations dans les provinces de l&#x2019;Equateur, Kinshasa et Tshopo, en RDC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to contribute to the reduction of morbidity and mortality due to the consequences on the health of populations affected by floods, in the six most impacted health zones of the three targeted provinces. This WHO project aims to strengthen alert systems and community engagement to prevent epidemics; improves access to essential health care for vulnerable populations, including mental health; reinforces epidemiological surveillance; and improves WASH measures in health facilities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 395,146 people, including 122,547 women, 158,245 children, and including 59,342 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
